ph is symmetric over the $y$-axis. This means that $cos⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡(-x)=cos⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $cos⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡(-x+18\\pi ) & =cos⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 9) \\\\  & =cos⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $cos⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡(-x) & =cos⁡x \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi cos⁡(-x+18\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pi \\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246035 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246036 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246037 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246038 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246039 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1041 "selection" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246035 13194139533675 true] [17592186246034 1110 #uuid "d6a4f6c9-a608-5d09-af9c-db72e6bf71d5" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246035 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533675 true] [17592186246035 1111 #uuid "2cb420bb-3d63-53ba-9980-bc74ae6cb5a3" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246036 1034 "1" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533675 true] [17592186246036 1111 #uuid "3dc323c8-b9be-5eb9-b6a6-5f1ce08e50e6" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246037 1034 "\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533675 true] [17592186246037 1111 #uuid "73e4ee61-8b56-5633-a858-b76c9d0bced6" 13194139533675 true] [17592186246038 1034 "2\\pi " 13194139533675 true] [17592186246038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533675 true] [17592186246038 1111